From 81d5818c2cc8a8cf78ca035175fe1eae43a88e12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garv <garvagnihotri22@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(onboarding): add import from VS Code, Cursor and
 Windsurf

- add IExtensionTransferService: copies settings.json,
  keybindings.json and the extensions folder from VS Code, Cursor or Windsurf into Loophole.
- an existing settings.json / keybindings.json is backed up as *.loophole-backup before it is overwritten,
  and extensions.json is merged, so what is already installed in Loophole is kept.
- skips remote, Copilot and other AI extensions, and the Kilo agent that Loophole already ships.
- returns what was imported and per-item errors, so the UI can say when an editor has nothing to import.
- only registered in the desktop build (workbench.desktop.main.ts); it needs the local file system.
